# ---- the main-red detector ignores stale GitHub runs pages (BH-1927, optional) ----
# GitHub's `actions/runs?branch=main` sometimes answers with a STALE page. On
# 2026-09-24 the hub read total_count=4355 with week-old runs, then 7094 on the
# very next call; the stale page carried two red monitor.yml pushes, so
# bin/main-red-detector.sh froze every merge lane on project-5 and paged
# --critical, and the next fresh page cleared it a minute later, for an hour.
#
# With the guard armed the detector keeps, per repo, the newest total_count and
# newest run created_at it has accepted in the coordination DB (`ledgers` row
# kind=main_red_runs, key=<owner>/<repo>). A page whose newest run is older
# decides nothing: no raise, no clear, no new-sha rewrite. A lower count with
# the same or a newer newest run is retention, not staleness, and is accepted. And before it raises a NEW flag it
# re-reads the page and raises only when the re-read picks the same arm,
# workflow and sha — one extra runs read on the tick a repo turns red, and the
# only guard left when the ledger cannot be reached.
#
# 1 is the default. Only the literal 0 disarms it, which is byte-for-byte the
# pre-BH-1927 detector: no ledger read or write and no second read.
#MAIN_RED_STALE_GUARD=1
